BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1b7120fc4ea00286@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221612Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Federal judge blocks attempts to restrict mai
 l-in voting
DESCRIPTION:AUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– A federal judge in Boston blocked the Tru
 mp administration from interfering with states’ rights to conduct mail-i
 n voting for the upcoming November elections\, now 67 days away. Judge Ind
 ira Talwani ruled yesterday that the plaintiffs were likely to succeed in 
 proving the administration’s order was unconstitutional.\n“Last night
 ’s decision was wonderful news for Maine voters who rely on absentee vot
 ing\,”\nSecretary Bellows said\n. “The judge made clear that the state
 s\, not the federal government\, are in charge of elections. That goes to
  the heart of our legal fights in court against the Trump Administration. 
 We will continue to stand with other states and voting rights advocates ac
 ross the nation to defend the voting rights – including the right to vot
 e by mail – for every citizen.”\nIn the decision\, Judge Talwani wrote
 \, “the Constitution charges the States with election administration” 
 going on to say that no law has been passed by Congress that “would perm
 it the USPS to regulate election mail.” The judge went even further to n
 ote that with just two months to the election\, it would an expensive and 
 likely impossible task for the 2026 election\, saying\, “Plaintiff State
 s face irreparable harm where they are required to comply with a likely un
 constitutional regulation for which compliance is practically impossible.
 ”\n###\nAttachment:\nread the 08-27-26 order\nhttps://www.maine.gov/sos/
 news/federal-judge-blocks-attempts-restrict-mail-voting
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/federal-judge-blocks-attempts-restrict-
 mail-voting
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
